  "description": "Typed, checked LLM results and agent tools for Microsoft.Extensions.AI IChatClient in C# and .NET. Use your configured chat client, such as Ollama or Azure OpenAI, with IntentSharp validation and bounded retries for invalid output. The backend and its configured adapters determine available models. UseChatClient and UseChatClientAsFallback select providers in code; the chat-client kind in a provider file selects a registered client. AsAIFunctions exposes catalog intents as AIFunction tools for Microsoft Agent Framework or another function-calling host: return a value after the intent checks pass, or an error result describing failure. The host executes function calls. Transport failures are not retried by IntentSharp; configure those retries in the chat-client pipeline or use a fallback. Installs the matching IntentSharp and IntentSharp.Catalog packages. Native OpenAI GPT or Anthropic Claude calls without IChatClient need only the core package. Commercial software, not open source: evaluate free for 30 days on development and test systems; after that, business use needs a paid license, and production use needs one from the first day (intentsharp.com/pricing).",
